column65:
If I'm not mistaken, that has the same semantics as the standard one line event definition, i.e.:<p><pre><code>    public event EventHandler MyEvent;
    // Inside the class, MyEvent is bound to a multicast delegate.
    // Outside the class, MyEvent is bound to an auto-generated add/remove mechanism.
    // So MyEvent can only be set to null or invoked from inside the class.</code></pre>
